# Integer16 comparison ordering

Verifies the int16 equality and ordering relations through the complete CLI
pipeline. Every operand is int16: comparisons are only defined between equal
types.

>>> source
low: int16 = -30000
high: int16 = 30000
same: int16 = 30000

// Verifies the equality family on equal and distinct operands.
print(high == same)
print(low == high)

// Verifies the ordering family on distinct operands.
print(low < high)
print(high < low)
print(high >= same)
print(low >= high)

<<< stdout
true
false
true
false
true
false

<<< stderr
